BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SF’s First Ever Halloween “Cookie Picnic” (Levi’s Plaza)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T150000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1638211@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Eating Drinking
DESCRIPTION:COOKIE PICNICThe sold-out Halloween 2026 Cookie Picnic takes p
 lace at Levi’s Plaza on November 1. Attendees bring two dozen homemade c
 ookies to share\, sample seasonal and Halloween-inspired bakes\, meet fell
 ow bakers\, and are encouraged to wear costumes.\nOriginal Event Descripti
 on:\nSan Francisco\, COOKIE PICNIC is here! And this time\, we’re making
  it Sweet and Spooky for Halloween weekend! 🍪🎃👻 Join us on Novemb
 er 1 for our first-ever Halloween-themed COOKIE PICNIC: a festive gatherin
 g filled with hundreds of homemade cookies\, creative costumes\, and plent
 y of treats to share. Start dreaming up your bake: brown butter pumpkin co
 okies\, caramel apple snickerdoodles\, black cocoa sandwich cookies\, spid
 erweb black sesame sugar cookies\, candy corn shortbread\, salted caramel 
 apple thumbprints\, or spooky chocolate chip cookies covered in candy eyes
 . Costumes are optional but highly encouraged. Come ready to celebrate Hal
 loween weekend\, meet fellow cookie lovers\, and see just how creative San
  Francisco’s bakers can get. Tickets are available now at www.cakepicnic
 tour.com/tickets! What Halloween cookie are you bringing? 🍁🍫🍎🧙
 🏼 What other city should we do a COOKIE PICNIC tour stop at? 🥰🤭 S
 an Francisco COOKIE PICNIC – Halloween 2026 Sun Nov 1\, 2026 1:00 PM –
  3:00 PM Levi’s Plaza\, 94111 Join waiting list Join waiting list Share 
 this event November 1: San Francisco COOKIE PICNIC Halloween isn’t over 
 quite yet! On November 1\, we’re bringing COOKIE PICNIC to San Francisco
  for one more sweet and...\n\n$57.50\n\nTickets: https://www.tickettailor.
 com/events/cakepicnictour/2402655?date=2026-11-01\nDetails: https://sf.fun
 cheap.com/sfs-halloween-cookie-picnic-levis-plaza/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/797472
 106_17947140519315793_7853608582892778223_n.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Levi’s Plaza\, 1255 Battery St\, San Francisco\, CA 94111
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-halloween-cookie-picnic-levis-plaza/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Halloween Pub Crawl: Dia De Los Muertos
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T180000
DTSTAMP:20261102T061947Z
UID:dothebay-17905482@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:2
CATEGORIES:Food & Drink
DESCRIPTION:CrawlSF Presents\nHalloween Pub Crawl: Dia De Los Muertos\nSun
 day\, November 1 | ​Mayes Oyster House\n\nMake Sunday\, November 1\, 202
 6\, a night to remember at CrawlSF’s Dia De Los Muertos Pub Crawl—the 
 spectacular closing chapter of the four-day Crawloween 2026 event.\n\nRunn
 ing from 4PM to 10PM\, this uniquely themed pub crawl lets you continue th
 e Halloween festivities while embracing the rich cultural traditions of D
 ía de los Muertos.\n\nCheck in at the historic Mayes Oyster House (1233 P
 olk Street\, San Francisco\, CA 94109) and gain free access to participati
 ng bars including Mayes\, McTeague’s\, El Lopo\, Wreck Room\, Uni Pizza\
 , Decodance\, Lush Lounge\, Beso Mae\, and more. Throughout the evening yo
 u’ll find drink specials\, DJs keeping the dance floors packed\, free pa
 rty favors\, lively contests\, and an atmosphere filled with celebration. 
 Feel free to rock your best Halloween costume or dress in respectful Día 
 de los Muertos style—traditional calavera face painting and attire are e
 ncouraged when worn to honor the holiday’s spirit of remembrance and joy
 .\n\nWhether you’re a longtime Crawloween fan or joining for the first t
 ime\, this final day offers the perfect mix of spooky fun and meaningful c
 ultural celebration across San Francisco’s Polk Street corridor and beyo
 nd.\n\nEvent Details:\nParticipating Bars: Mayes\, Union Street Ale House\
 , The Blue Light\, Sacred Taco\, Route 101\, Palm House\, The Brixton\, Co
 met Club\, White Rabbit\, Marina Greens\, Mcteagues\, Music City Star Fact
 ory\, Rockwell\, Jaxson\,...\n\n$12 - $35\, 21+\nCrawlSF Presents\n\nDetai
 ls: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/1/halloween-pub-crawl-dia-de-los-m
 uertos-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.788296;-122.4205566
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34721638/d3060885-a7ac-4232-a1c7-bcfafa62f23a.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261102T061947Z
LOCATION:Mayes Oyster House\, 1233 Polk St.\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/1/halloween-pub-crawl-dia-de-los-m
 uertos-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sprouts' Annual Gala: Powerful Women in Food
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T190000
DTSTAMP:20261102T061947Z
UID:dothebay-17690941@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Food & Drink
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable evening featuring welcome bubbles
 \, cocktails\, chef-crafted bites\, and an exceptional four-course dinner 
 by Michelin-starred and award-winning women chefs\, alongside honorary gue
 sts Alice Waters of Chez Panisse and Debby Soo\, CEO of OpenTable. Savor e
 xpertly paired wines\, exclusive VIP experiences\, and a live auction host
 ed by Emmy Award-winning broadcaster Liam Mayclem.\n\nCity View at Metreon
  | November 1\, 2026\n\nCulinary Talent:\n\nChef Carrie Blease | Wolfsbane
 \nChef Azalina Eusope | Azalina's\nChef Danielle Lefevre | Trestle SF\nChe
 f Belinda Leong | B. Patisserie\nChef Nancy Oakes | Boulevard\nChef Laura 
 Ozyilmaz | Dalida\nChef Melissa Perello | Frances & Octavia\nChef Gayle Pi
 rie | Foreign Cinema\nChef Pim Techamuanvivit | Nari\nChef Dana S. Younkin
  | Boulevard\n\nThis special evening will celebrate Powerful Women in Food
  while supporting Sprouts Chef Training’s mission to empower aspiring Ba
 y Area Youth through culinary training\, mentorship\, and career opportuni
 ties. ‍\n\nEvent Co-Chairs: Tommy Halvorson\, Michael Bauer\nEvent Produ
 ction: Foxtail Events\nSprouts Chef Training is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit. 70%
  of each ticket is tax-deductible.\n\nFor ticket inquiries or general even
 t questions please contact: julias@sproutscheftraining.org\n\nTickets from
  $650\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/1/sprouts-annual-gal
 a-powerful-women-in-food-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
